-- the journal of a change to the source (part of language-implementation-remainder). A change
-- records new text, has it checked, and puts the old text back if it does not check; a process
-- stopped between the first and the last left the unchecked text in the source, read again by
-- every later change (2026-11-22: two statements whose checks did not end were left so, and every
-- write after them ran their checks). So the intent is written first: for every path of the
-- change its old text (or nothing, for a path that held nothing), then the mark naming the paths
-- (the mark present means the texts are whole); it is forgotten when the change is kept or put
-- back; and the next action that takes the write lock, finding the mark, puts every path back
-- before doing anything else. One change is a list of paths; a change to one file is the list of
-- one
hy-intend : List Word → List (List Word × Sum Unit (List Word)) → Proc W Unit
hy-intend st es = bind (hy-intend-texts st es) (λ u → bind (h-write (hy-pend-mark st) (h-concat (list-map (λ e → h-line (fst e)) es))) (λ b → ret unit))
